    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 5.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>Et constituerunt, monetarii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="52" target="#IVAtr_5-3.lnote.oe.52"/> cur manum perdant, et ponatur super ipsius monete fabricam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="74" ed="#robertson"/>Et constituerunt, monetarii cur<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#IVAtr_5-3.robnote.fn.15"/> manum perdant et ponatur super ipsius monetae fabricam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Und sie haben festgesetzt, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.1"/> [Falsch]münzer die Hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.2"/> verlieren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.3"/>, und diese über jener Münzschmiede angebracht werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And they have established that [false] moneyers lose their hand, and that it be fixed over that mint.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_5-3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="75" ed="#robertson"/>And they have decreed that<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_5-3.robnote.n.2"/> coiners shall lose a hand, and that it shall be fastened up over the mint.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IVAtr_9-1">IV Atr 9.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><ref target="clause:IICn_8-1">II Cn 8.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.lnote.oe.52" n="52" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cur mo. <hi rend="italic">MHk;</hi> quod mo. <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cur mo. MHk; quod mo. Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Original stand wohl <hi rend="italic">þa</hi> im demonstrativen Sinne ‘jene’, was Q als Artikel verkannte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The original probably had <hi rend="italic">þa</hi> in the demonstrative sense ‘those’, which Q mistook for the article</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verstümmelung ist zwar wie Todesstrafe in 5, 4 auch Abspaltung der Friedlosigkeit. Aber die Nebeneinanderstellung verschiedener Grade der Leibesstrafe erklärt sich doch nur durch Benutzung zweier Vorlagen. Auch in VI As (<hi rend="italic">s</hi>. dazu Einl. n. 6) kombinierte ein Londoner Stadtschreiber Widersprechendes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Mutilation, it is true, like the death penalty in 5, 4, is also an offshoot of outlawry. But the juxtaposition of different degrees of corporal punishment can surely be explained only by the use of two sources. In VI As too (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> on this Introduction n. 6) a London town clerk combined contradictory material</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies neben anderem benutzt II Cn 8, 1 = Hn 13, 3; <hi rend="italic">þolige handa</hi> übs. Q dort ebenso; er las das also wohl im Or. auch dieser Stelle</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">II Cn 8, 1 = Hn 13, 3 uses this, among other things; Q translates <hi rend="italic">þolige handa</hi> in the same way there; so he probably read this in the orig. of this passage too</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 14, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II Atr. 1 Q.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_5-3.robnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>cur</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">cur mon.</hi> M, Hk; <hi rend="italic">quod mon.</hi> Br.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
